Key takeaway: Interrupting the NETs-CD44-IL-17A feedback loop may be a potential therapeutic target for Behçet's uveitis, as it drives Th17-mediated inflammation through neutrophil infiltration and hyperactivation.", "url": "https://consensus.app/papers/nets‐cd44‐il‐17a-feedback-loop-drives-th17‐mediated-wu-ning/119a7a5358b15707a770aca764cea78f/?utm_source=chatgpt", "metadata": {"authors": "Yi Wu, K. Ning, Zhao-Hao Huang, Bin-Yao Chen, Jun-Jie Chen, Ying-Ying Wen, J. Bu, Han Hong, Qiaorong Chen, Zhuo-Qi Zhang, Renbing Jia, Wen-Ru Su", "publish_year": "2025", "journal": "Advanced Science", "volume": "12", "citation_count": "23", "doi": "10.1002/advs.202411524"}}
